# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Jia Bi et al. (2026). A budget-dependent crossover between coverage- and response-based training-set selection for machine-learned interatomic potentials.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2609.05877  arXiv:2609.05877v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2609.05877v1 (sha256 46b46a2a5706f204...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 456 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/bi2026budget.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: fixed 1,400-structure panels from the GAP-20 carbon
# archive and pooled rMD17 (1,000 training, 200 validation, 200 test),
# MACE models retrained on subsets chosen by Random, FPS/DPP coverage or
# a response witness at 1, 5 and 20 % budgets, and the held-out mean
# force-vector errors at the 20 % budget and for the full-data reference
# (Table 2, 'Mean' endpoint; five-seed means). Absolute gaps, other
# endpoints and the HEA25/MACE-MP-0 diagnostics are figure- or SI-level.

